  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nCold front will cross the region from NW to SE Friday morning,\npreceded and accompanied by some rain showers across the SW\nAdirondacks before weakening. Isolated showers/sprinkles may \nextend farther south and east into the Capital Region, however \nwill remain much more limited in coverage. In the wake of the \ncold frontal passage, gusty northwest winds are expected to \ndevelop with gusts reaching 25-35 mph late Friday morning into \nthe afternoon hours. RH values will drop to 35-45 percent within\nlower elevations of the Hudson Valley and NW CT, and 45-55 \npercent within slightly higher elevations of the Helderbergs, \neastern Catskills, Taconics, Berkshires and Litchfield Hills. \nIn collaboration with NYS/New England DEC's/DEP's and \nsurrounding WFO's, given the drying fuels across these areas \nwith little or no rainfall over the last 7+ days, a Special \nWeather Statement has been issued for 11 AM-6 PM Friday for \nelevated risk of fire spread.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nDry weather is expected this weekend through the middle of next\nweek, outside the very low chance of showers with a passing\nfrontal system Tuesday-Wednesday. Temperatures should initially\nbe near normal this weekend, trending above normal next week. A\nstronger frontal system and approaching deep upper level trough\nfrom the west may bring widespread rainfall for next Thursday \nor Friday.",
